# wiki-paths — a wiki page's type, path and name

POLICY wiki-paths-placement:
    ABOUT    which folders and root files hold wiki pages
    APPLIES  #wiki-placement

    ALWAYS  put a page in the one folder of its type: wiki/sources/, wiki/entities/, wiki/concepts/ or wiki/syntheses/
    ALWAYS  keep wiki/index.md and wiki/log.md as the only content files at the wiki root
    ALWAYS  write a page's frontmatter as page-frontmatter says, a wiki/index.md line as index-line says
    ALWAYS  write a wiki/log.md entry as log-entry says
    NEVER   create a folder or subfolder without the user's approval

POLICY wiki-paths-naming:
    ABOUT    what a wiki file is called
    APPLIES  #wiki-naming

    ALWAYS  name a file in lowercase kebab-case, after its subject as a singular canonical noun phrase
    NEVER   put a type prefix or version suffix in a file name, or a date outside wiki/sources/
    ALWAYS  name a page in wiki/sources/ after its raw file — raw/YYYY-MM-DD-slug.ext is wiki/sources/YYYY-MM-DD-slug.md
    ALWAYS  keep every basename unique across the whole vault — Obsidian [[wikilinks]] resolve by basename
    ALWAYS  give each subject at most one page — a synonym goes in the aliases of that page
    ALWAYS  name and scope a page at the level people recognize at once — no broad umbrella, no narrow instance

POLICY wiki-paths-justification:
    ABOUT    what earns a category or a page its place, and how categories are chosen
    APPLIES  #wiki-justification

    NEVER   add a category that no real document justifies
    ALWAYS  open a page in wiki/entities/ or wiki/concepts/ only for a subject in two sources or more, or central to one
    ALWAYS  treat a subject as central to a source when it is in the source's title or has its own heading there
    ALWAYS  choose and order wiki/index.md categories by how people look for things, never by abstract subject logic

POLICY wiki-paths-classification:
    ABOUT    how a page is classified: one verifiable type by folder, anything further by attributes
    APPLIES  #wiki-classification

    ALWAYS  give every page exactly one type
    ALWAYS  type a subject's page as entity when it has a proper name and a single referent, as concept otherwise
    ALWAYS  decide a page's type by criteria two people would apply the same way
    NEVER   let a page's type depend on anything that changes over time
    ALWAYS  describe any further dimension with an independent frontmatter attribute
    NEVER   introduce free-form tags

TEMPLATE page-frontmatter:
    ABOUT  the frontmatter of a wiki page
    SLOTS:
        type:      ENUM[source, entity, concept, synthesis]  "the page's type"
        updated:   TEXT  "the date of the last change, as YYYY-MM-DD"
        sources?:  TEXT  "the source pages behind it; not on a source page"
        raw?:      TEXT  "the path of its raw file; only on a source page"
        aliases?:  TEXT  "the other names of its subject"

TEMPLATE index-line:
    ABOUT  one line of wiki/index.md
    SLOTS:
        line:  TEXT  "`- [[page]] — one-line summary`, under the heading of its category"

TEMPLATE log-entry:
    ABOUT  one entry of wiki/log.md
    SLOTS:
        entry:  TEXT  "`## [YYYY-MM-DD] ingest|query|lint | Title`"

TEMPLATE page-path:
    ABOUT  the path a new page takes
    SLOTS:
        path:  TEXT  "the page's path from the project root"

TEMPLATE page-path-request:
    ABOUT  what is needed to derive the path of a new page
    SLOTS:
        type:   ENUM[source, entity, concept, synthesis]  "the page's type"
        slug:   TEXT  "the page's file name, without extension"
        taken?:  TEXT  "every basename already in the vault, comma-separated"

TEMPLATE wiki-state:
    ABOUT  the wiki and the raw files as they are now, for a program to read
    SLOTS:
        pages:  TEXT  "every file of wiki/ with its full text, each opening with a line `=== <path>`"
        raw:    TEXT  "every path under raw/, one per line"

TEMPLATE page-match:
    ABOUT  the page a subject already has, by name or alias
    SLOTS:
        path?:  TEXT  "the page's path, absent when no name or alias matches"

TEMPLATE page-move-request:
    ABOUT  which page to move or rename, and where
    SLOTS:
        old_name:  TEXT  "the page's basename now"
        new_name:  TEXT  "its new basename"
        folder?:   ENUM[wiki/sources/, wiki/entities/, wiki/concepts/, wiki/syntheses/]  "its new folder, if it changes"
        date:      TEXT  "today, as YYYY-MM-DD"

TEMPLATE page-move-plan:
    ABOUT  every edit a move or a rename needs
    SLOTS:
        from:       TEXT  "the page's path now"
        to:         TEXT  "the page's new path"
        rewritten:  TEXT  "every file that changes, with its new full text, each opening with a line `=== <path>`"
        log_entry:  TEXT  "the entry to append to wiki/log.md"

TEMPLATE wiki-findings:
    ABOUT  what the mechanical checks of the wiki found
    SLOTS:
        errors?:    TEXT  "what breaks a rule for certain, one `<path>: <problem>` per line"
        warnings?:  TEXT  "what the agent has to judge, one `<path>: <problem>` per line"

TEMPLATE label-tables:
    ABOUT  the three tables to join, as `store q` prints them
    SLOTS:
        files:   TEXT  "every record of wiki-files, one per line"
        labels:  TEXT  "every record of wiki-labels, one per line"
        links?:  TEXT  "every record of wiki-file-labels, one per line"

TEMPLATE file-labels:
    ABOUT  every wiki file joined with its labels
    SLOTS:
        rows:         TEXT  "one `<path> | <label> | <label description>` per line"
        unlabelled?:  TEXT  "the files with no label, one path per line"
        broken?:      TEXT  "the links to a file or a label that does not exist, one per line"

VAR path-request AS page-path-request
VAR label-data AS label-tables
VAR labelled-files AS file-labels
VAR new-page-path AS page-path
VAR wiki-now AS wiki-state
VAR page-subject
VAR existing-page AS page-match
VAR move-request AS page-move-request
VAR move-plan AS page-move-plan
VAR structure-findings AS wiki-findings

COMPUTE derive-page-path:
    ABOUT  the path of a new page, from its type, its file name and the basenames already taken
    NEVER  read a file, the network or the clock
    REQUIRE:
        MUST  the slug of {{path-request}} be absent from its taken names
    RETURN AS page-path:
        DO    path = the folder of the type of {{path-request}} + its slug + .md
    ENSURE:
        MUST  path sit directly in wiki/sources/, wiki/entities/, wiki/concepts/ or wiki/syntheses/

COMPUTE find-existing-page:
    ABOUT  the page whose name or aliases match a subject exactly
    NEVER  read a file, the network or the clock
    REQUIRE:
        MUST  {{page-subject}} be a kebab-case name, and {{wiki-now}} hold the wiki's pages
    RETURN AS page-match:
        DO    path = the page of {{wiki-now}} whose basename or aliases equal {{page-subject}}
    ENSURE:
        MUST  path be absent when nothing matches exactly

COMPUTE plan-page-move:
    ABOUT  every edit a move or a rename needs, computed and not applied
    NEVER  read a file, the network or the clock
    REQUIRE:
        MUST  the old name of {{move-request}} be a page of {{wiki-now}}
        MUST  its new name be taken by no page of {{wiki-now}}, and be lowercase kebab-case
    RETURN AS page-move-plan:
        DO    add the old name to the aliases of the page in {{wiki-now}}
        DO    rewrite every wikilink and wiki/index.md entry pointing to the old name
        DO    write the entry to append to wiki/log.md
    ENSURE:
        MUST  no wikilink to the old name be left in rewritten

COMPUTE check-wiki-structure:
    ABOUT  the checks of the wiki's structure that need no judgment
    NEVER  read a file, the network or the clock
    REQUIRE:
        MUST  {{wiki-now}} hold the wiki's pages
    RETURN AS wiki-findings:
        DO    errors = folders and root files not allowed, `type` missing or not matching its folder
        DO    errors += file names breaking the naming rules, repeated basenames, aliases that collide
        DO    errors += `raw:` paths not in {{wiki-now}}, free-form tags, broken wikilinks
        DO    errors += pages and wiki/index.md entries that do not match, malformed wiki/log.md entries
        DO    warnings = entity and concept pages with fewer than two sources, close names, plural-looking names
    ENSURE:
        MUST  every line name the path it is about

COMPUTE join-files-labels:
    ABOUT  every wiki file joined with its labels and their descriptions
    NEVER  read a file, the network or the clock
    REQUIRE:
        MUST  every record of {{label-data}} be a line of key=value fields, as `store q` prints it
    RETURN AS file-labels:
        DO    join the files and the labels of {{label-data}} through its links, on path and on label
    ENSURE:
        MUST  every file be in rows or in unlabelled, and every link that matches nothing be in broken

PROCEDURE show-file-labels:
    ABOUT  show which labels each wiki file has
    DO  read all records of wiki-files, wiki-labels and wiki-file-labels with limit=100000 INTO label-data
    RUN  join-files-labels INTO labelled-files
    DO  report the rows, the unlabelled files and the broken links

PROCEDURE gather-wiki-state:
    ABOUT  read the wiki and the raw paths, for a program
    DO  read every file of wiki/ and list every path under raw/ INTO wiki-now

@WITH wiki-paths-placement, wiki-paths-naming, wiki-paths-justification
@WITH wiki-paths-classification
PROCEDURE choose-new-page-path:
    ABOUT  choose the path of a new page
    RUN  gather-wiki-state
    DO  name the page's subject in kebab-case INTO page-subject
    RUN  find-existing-page INTO existing-page
    IF no page matched, and an existing page covers the subject under another name:
        DO  add the name to that page's aliases, and use that page's path
    ELSE IF a page matched:
        DO  use that page's path
    ELSE
        IF the page's type is uncertain:
            RUN  resolve-boundary-case
        IF the type is entity or concept, and the subject is in fewer than two sources and central to none:
            DO  put the content in a section of an existing page, and derive no new path
        ELSE
            DO  store the page's type, its file name and every basename in the vault INTO path-request
            RUN  derive-page-path INTO new-page-path

@WITH wiki-paths-placement, wiki-paths-classification
PROCEDURE handle-unplaced-page:
    ABOUT  handle a page that fits no type or seems to need a new folder
    DO  ask the user for approval before adding a type or a folder

@WITH wiki-paths-placement, wiki-paths-naming
PROCEDURE move-or-rename-page:
    ABOUT  move or rename a page
    RUN  gather-wiki-state
    DO  state the page's old name, its new name and any new folder INTO move-request
    RUN  plan-page-move INTO move-plan
    DO  apply the plan as it is: move the file, write each rewritten file, append the log entry

@WITH wiki-paths-classification
PROCEDURE resolve-boundary-case:
    ABOUT  settle the type of a page that could plausibly be of two types
    DO  compare the page with typical pages of each candidate type
    IF wiki/log.md records a decision on a similar page:
        DO  follow that decision
    ELSE
        DO  ask the user which type the page is
        DO  record the decision and its reason in wiki/log.md, so that later similar pages go the same way

@WITH wiki-paths-placement, wiki-paths-naming, wiki-paths-justification
@WITH wiki-paths-classification
PROCEDURE review-wiki-structure:
    ABOUT  report what no longer fits and propose merges or moves
    MUST-NOT  move, merge, rename or restructure anything without the user's approval
    RUN  gather-wiki-state
    RUN  check-wiki-structure INTO structure-findings
    DO  judge each warning in structure-findings, and keep those that hold
    DO  look for pages hard to place, types that hide content, and pages failing a judgment rule
    DO  report every error and each finding kept, with its proposed merge or move
    IF the user approves a merge or a move:
        RUN  move-or-rename-page

STORE wiki-files:
    ABOUT  every file of the wiki: where it is and what it holds
    DRIVER tabeli
    LASTS  project
    KEY    path
    SLOTS:
        path:         TEXT                "the file's path from the project root"
        description:  TEXT MAX_WORDS 30   "what the file holds"

STORE wiki-labels:
    ABOUT  the labels available for wiki files, and what each one means
    DRIVER tabeli
    LASTS  project
    KEY    label
    SLOTS:
        label:        TEXT               "the label, as one lowercase kebab-case word group"
        description:  TEXT MAX_WORDS 30  "what files with this label hold"

STORE wiki-file-labels:
    ABOUT  which wiki file has which label, one record per pair
    DRIVER tabeli
    LASTS  project
    KEY    link
    SLOTS:
        link:   TEXT  "the pair, as `<path>#<label>`"
        path:   TEXT  "the file's path, as in wiki-files"
        label:  TEXT  "the label, as in wiki-labels"

EXPORT SKILL wiki-paths:
    ABOUT    Decides a wiki page's type, path and name — load it to create, move or rename a page, or to lint the wiki
    APPLIES  #wiki
    MANDATE  give each justified page one type and path, keep its links intact when it changes, and report misfits

    WHEN choosing the path of a new page:
        RUN  choose-new-page-path

    WHEN a page fits none of the four types, or seems to need a new folder:
        RUN  handle-unplaced-page

    WHEN moving or renaming a page:
        RUN  move-or-rename-page

    WHEN a page could plausibly be of two types:
        RUN  resolve-boundary-case

    WHEN a wiki lint or a structural review is requested:
        RUN  review-wiki-structure

    WHEN asked which labels the wiki files have, or which files have a label:
        RUN  show-file-labels

    WHEN a wiki file is created, moved, renamed or deleted, or what it holds changes:
        IN wiki-files:
            DO  keep exactly one record per existing wiki file, with its current path and description
        IN wiki-file-labels:
            DO  keep one record per label of each existing wiki file, with its current path
